<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Teutonic War (1519–1521)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Cavalry War, Reiterkrieg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Teutonic War of 1519–1521 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> under Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia">Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, who refused homage to the Polish king. Polish forces devastated much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, and the Order received little help from the Empire. A four-year truce was agreed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a> in 1521, and in 1525 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-krakow">Treaty of Kraków</a> turned the Order's state into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a>.</p></div>
